# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Astronomy Open Night 2026 — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` and pass with:
#   flutter run --dart-define-from-file=.env
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠️  THE APP RUNS WITH NO KEYS — navigation degrades gracefully.
#
# `flutter run` works with no .env file at all. Every screen runs on
# data compiled into the binary, and the campus map is the app's own
# illustrated basemap (no tile service, no OpenStreetMap, no key). The
# only feature that needs keys is Google Maps walking directions: without
# them, the Directions screen shows a clear "not configured yet" message
# instead of a map (never a crash, never a fake route).
#
# This file exists to (a) document that absence deliberately, so nobody
# assumes a missing key is why something is broken, and (b) give the
# variables a home.
#
# Do NOT copy values from the MQ Journey repository into here. That
# project's Supabase, Firebase and Transport for NSW credentials belong
# to a different product and must not be reused.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Build environment label. One of: development | staging | production
APP_ENV=development

# ── Google Maps: ONE key drives everything ─────────────────
# Astronomy uses Google Maps as the ONLY navigation provider, walking
# mode only, scoped to the Macquarie University campus. Three variables,
# but a SINGLE Google Cloud API key may fill all three for local testing
# (production should use per-platform restricted keys — see
# docs/google-maps-setup.md).
#
#   MAPS_API_KEY                    → the native interactive map (tiles,
#                                     markers, polyline). Read by Dart
#                                     (--dart-define), by the Android build
#                                     (into the manifest), and handed to iOS
#                                     GMSServices at consent time. Presence
#                                     of this key is what enables the flow.
#   GOOGLE_MAPS_ANDROID_ROUTES_KEY  → the Routes API call (walking route
#   GOOGLE_MAPS_IOS_ROUTES_KEY        polyline + distance + ETA), per platform.
#
# Leave all three blank to ship "dark": the app builds and runs, and the
# Directions screen shows "Google Maps is not configured yet."
#
# APIs to enable in Google Cloud: Maps SDK for Android, Maps SDK for iOS,
# Routes API. See docs/google-maps-setup.md for restrictions & rotation.

MAPS_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_MAPS_ANDROID_ROUTES_KEY=
GOOGLE_MAPS_IOS_ROUTES_KEY=

# ── Web ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The web build does NOT read MAPS_API_KEY from here. To show the Google
# map on web, uncomment the Maps JavaScript API script tag in
# web/index.html with a browser-restricted key. Left commented by default,
# the web build ships without the interactive Google map (see the setup doc).

# ── Deliberately absent ────────────────────────────────────
# There is no auth, no user accounts, no analytics and no backend in
# this MVP, so there are no keys for any of them. If you find yourself
# adding one, that is a scope change worth discussing first — see
# docs/project-scope.md.
